#' MCD-Based Robust Correlation Matrix
#'
#' @description
#' Computes a robust correlation matrix using the Minimum Covariance Determinant
#' (MCD) estimator for the covariance matrix.
#'
#' @param x Numeric matrix or data frame
#'
#' @details
#' The function:
#' \enumerate{
#'   \item Computes the MCD robust covariance matrix using \code{\link{DetMCD}}
#'   \item Converts the covariance matrix to a correlation matrix using \code{cov2cor}
#' }
#'
#' The MCD estimator is a highly robust estimator of multivariate location and
#' scatter, providing resistance to outliers. The resulting correlation matrix
#' is more resistant to outlying observations than the classical Pearson correlation.
#'
#' @return
#' Robust correlation matrix (same dimensions as ncol(x) × ncol(x))
#'
#' @seealso \code{\link{DetMCD}}, \code{\link{wincor}}, \code{\link{pbcor}}
#'
#' @keywords multivariate robust
#' @export
MCDCOR<-function(x){
#val<-cov.mcd(x)
val<-DetMCD(x)
val=cov2cor(val$cov)
val
}




