#' Zonoid Data Depth
#'
#' @description
#' Computes zonoid data depth for multivariate data. Wrapper for
#' \code{ddalpha::depth.zonoid} with argument naming consistent with other
#' WRS depth functions.
#'
#' @param x Matrix or data frame of observations (rows = observations, columns = variables).
#' @param pts Matrix of points at which to evaluate depth (default: same as \code{x}).
#' @param SEED Logical. Included for compatibility with classification functions (not used).
#'
#' @details
#' Zonoid depth is a multivariate depth measure based on zonoid geometry.
#' Points in the center of the data cloud have higher depth. The method is
#' affine-equivariant and generalizes the univariate quantile concept.
#'
#' Requires the \pkg{ddalpha} package.
#'
#' @return Numeric vector of zonoid depth values, one for each row of \code{pts}.
#'   Values range from 0 (low depth, outlying) to 1 (high depth, central).
#'
#' @references
#' Dyckerhoff, R., Koshevoy, G., and Mosler, K. (1996). Zonoid data depth:
#' theory and computation. In: Prat A. (ed), \emph{COMPSTAT 1996. Proceedings in
#' computational statistics}, Physica-Verlag (Heidelberg), 235-240.
#'
#' Koshevoy, G. and Mosler, K. (1997). Zonoid trimming for multivariate
#' distributions. \emph{Annals of Statistics}, 25, 1998-2017.
#'
#' @seealso \code{\link[ddalpha]{depth.zonoid}}, \code{\link{spat}}, \code{\link{Doplot}}
#'
#' @export
#' @keywords multivariate robust
zonoid<-function(x,pts=x,SEED=TRUE){
#
#   Requires  ddalpha
#
#  SEED, included for convenience when this function is used with certain classification techniques.
#
#  Compute zonoid depths
#  Dyckerhoff, R., Koshevoy, G., and Mosler, K. (1996).
#  Zonoid data depth: theory and computation.
#  In: Prat A. (ed), COMPSTAT 1996. Proceedings in computational
#   statistics, Physica-Verlag (Heidelberg), 235--240.

# Koshevoy, G. and Mosler, K. (1997). Zonoid trimming
# for multivariate distributions Annals of Statistics 25 1998--2017.
# The code was written by Rainer Dyckerhoff.
#
#  This function is for convenience: The arguments are consistent with
#  other depth functions in Rallfun and the R package WRS
#
library(ddalpha)
depth.zonoid(pts,x)
}




